      "id": "mount_failure_recovery_bcb",
      "fact": "Actual init/builtins.cpp can call wipe_data_via_recovery for FS_MGR_MNTALL_DEV_NEEDS_RECOVERY; it constructs --wipe_data, writes BCB and requests reboot. Removing recovery/uncrypt/applypatch packages does not remove this compiled init path. Current SD fstab still contains check/encryptable. Exact BCB device resolution, malformed-media behavior and internal-storage preservation need integration review/tests. No assertion that this branch was executed or wrote the physical device."
    },
    {
      "id": "usb_vold_paths",
      "fact": "SD fstab retains /devices/ff580000.usb*, ff5c0000, ff5d0000 and /devices/usb*, while pinned RK322x DTS USB controllers use addresses30040000,30080000,300a0000,300c0000,300e0000,30100000,30120000. Actual kernel uevent/vold matching must be traced before claiming USB media discovery; DocumentsUI packages alone do not prove it."
    },
    {
      "id": "device_permissions_selinux",
      "fact": "Minimal board init only mounts the SD fstab when ro.bootmode=sd; vendor graphics device-node ownership, ueventd/SELinux, services and full mount ordering are not integrated."
